{"blocks":[["Ableton/Live/UG/41%20Accessibility%20and%20Keyboard%20Nav/04%20Navigating%20in%20Live/01%20Navigate%20Menu/","source-block-136","41.4.1 Navigate Menu",[]],["Ableton/Live/UG/41%20Accessibility%20and%20Keyboard%20Nav/04%20Navigating%20in%20Live/01%20Navigate%20Menu/","source-block-259","The Navigate menu reaches every main view, and most entries have a shortcut. Open it with VO+M then N under VoiceOver (Mac), or Alt+N (Win).",["41.4.1 Navigate Menu"]],["Ableton/Live/UG/41%20Accessibility%20and%20Keyboard%20Nav/04%20Navigating%20in%20Live/01%20Navigate%20Menu/","source-block-409","41.4.1.1 Control Bar — Option+0 (Mac) / Alt+0 (Win)",["41.4.1 Navigate Menu"]],["Ableton/Live/UG/41%20Accessibility%20and%20Keyboard%20Nav/04%20Navigating%20in%20Live/01%20Navigate%20Menu/","source-block-473","The Ableton/Live/UI/Control Bar groups project settings, transport, tools and status views. Tab through the groups with Speak Help Text on to hear what each does. Focus returns to the last control used.",["41.4.1 Navigate Menu","41.4.1.1 Control Bar — Option+0 (Mac) / Alt+0 (Win)"]],["Ableton/Live/UG/41%20Accessibility%20and%20Keyboard%20Nav/04%20Navigating%20in%20Live/01%20Navigate%20Menu/","source-block-686","41.4.1.2 Session View — Option+1 (Mac) / Alt+1 (Win)",["41.4.1 Navigate Menu"]],["Ableton/Live/UG/41%20Accessibility%20and%20Keyboard%20Nav/04%20Navigating%20in%20Live/01%20Navigate%20Menu/","source-block-751","Track title bars — left and right arrows move between them; right-click for track commands.",["41.4.1 Navigate Menu","41.4.1.2 Session View — Option+1 (Mac) / Alt+1 (Win)"]],["Ableton/Live/UG/41%20Accessibility%20and%20Keyboard%20Nav/04%20Navigating%20in%20Live/01%20Navigate%20Menu/","source-block-853","Clip slots — tracks run top to bottom, scenes left to right. Cmd+Shift+M (Mac) / Ctrl+Shift+M (Win) inserts an empty MIDI clip; Enter launches the selected clip, following the Ableton/Live/UI/Control Bar/Menu/Quantization setting. Return tracks show slots that cannot hold clips.",["41.4.1 Navigate Menu","41.4.1.2 Session View — Option+1 (Mac) / Alt+1 (Win)"]],["Ableton/Live/UG/41%20Accessibility%20and%20Keyboard%20Nav/04%20Navigating%20in%20Live/01%20Navigate%20Menu/","source-block-1153","Scenes — up and down arrows move between Main track scene numbers; Enter launches a scene.",["41.4.1 Navigate Menu","41.4.1.2 Session View — Option+1 (Mac) / Alt+1 (Win)"]],["Ableton/Live/UG/41%20Accessibility%20and%20Keyboard%20Nav/04%20Navigating%20in%20Live/01%20Navigate%20Menu/","source-block-1256","Mixer — choose which mixer sections show from View → Mixer Controls or the menu by the Mixer view control at the bottom right. Crossfader, track options and performance impact are hidden by default.",["41.4.1 Navigate Menu","41.4.1.2 Session View — Option+1 (Mac) / Alt+1 (Win)"]],["Ableton/Live/UG/41%20Accessibility%20and%20Keyboard%20Nav/04%20Navigating%20in%20Live/01%20Navigate%20Menu/","source-block-1467","Tab / Shift+Tab move from slots to the mixer and through a track's mixer controls. Next Neighbor and Previous Neighbor, Option+Tab / Option+Shift+Tab (Mac), move to the same control on another track. Esc returns to the track's title bar.",["41.4.1 Navigate Menu","41.4.1.2 Session View — Option+1 (Mac) / Alt+1 (Win)"]],["Ableton/Live/UG/41%20Accessibility%20and%20Keyboard%20Nav/04%20Navigating%20in%20Live/01%20Navigate%20Menu/","source-block-1719","41.4.1.3 Arrangement View — Option+2 (Mac) / Alt+2 (Win)",["41.4.1 Navigate Menu"]],["Ableton/Live/UG/41%20Accessibility%20and%20Keyboard%20Nav/04%20Navigating%20in%20Live/01%20Navigate%20Menu/","source-block-1788","In Ableton/Live/UI/Arrangement View:",["41.4.1 Navigate Menu","41.4.1.3 Arrangement View — Option+2 (Mac) / Alt+2 (Win)"]],["Ableton/Live/UG/41%20Accessibility%20and%20Keyboard%20Nav/04%20Navigating%20in%20Live/01%20Navigate%20Menu/","source-block-1833","Tracks — up and down arrows move between tracks; Option+Tab (Mac) moves between track mixers, and Tab / Shift+Tab through a mixer's controls.",["41.4.1 Navigate Menu","41.4.1.3 Arrangement View — Option+2 (Mac) / Alt+2 (Win)"]],["Ableton/Live/UG/41%20Accessibility%20and%20Keyboard%20Nav/04%20Navigating%20in%20Live/01%20Navigate%20Menu/","source-block-1991","Timeline — left and right arrows step by the grid; + and - widen or narrow the grid; Option plus left or right (Mac) jumps to the previous or next clip edge or locator.",["41.4.1 Navigate Menu","41.4.1.3 Arrangement View — Option+2 (Mac) / Alt+2 (Win)"]],["Ableton/Live/UG/41%20Accessibility%20and%20Keyboard%20Nav/04%20Navigating%20in%20Live/01%20Navigate%20Menu/","source-block-2176","Locators — arrow to a spot, Tab to Ableton/Live/UI/Arrangement View/Button/Set Locator and press Enter; Tab / Shift+Tab move between locators; Delete removes one.",["41.4.1 Navigate Menu","41.4.1.3 Arrangement View — Option+2 (Mac) / Alt+2 (Win)"]],["Ableton/Live/UG/41%20Accessibility%20and%20Keyboard%20Nav/04%20Navigating%20in%20Live/01%20Navigate%20Menu/","source-block-2363","Content — Shift plus arrows selects; arrows move the selection; Cmd+X, Cmd+C, Cmd+V, Cmd+D and Delete cut, copy, paste, duplicate and delete (Ctrl on Windows).",["41.4.1 Navigate Menu","41.4.1.3 Arrangement View — Option+2 (Mac) / Alt+2 (Win)"]],["Ableton/Live/UG/41%20Accessibility%20and%20Keyboard%20Nav/04%20Navigating%20in%20Live/01%20Navigate%20Menu/","source-block-2547","Clip edges — put the insert marker on an edge, press Enter, adjust with the arrows, then Enter to confirm or Esc to cancel.",["41.4.1 Navigate Menu","41.4.1.3 Arrangement View — Option+2 (Mac) / Alt+2 (Win)"]],["Ableton/Live/UG/41%20Accessibility%20and%20Keyboard%20Nav/04%20Navigating%20in%20Live/01%20Navigate%20Menu/","source-block-2687","Export — select a region and press Cmd+R (Mac) / Ctrl+R (Win); the Main track renders by default.",["41.4.1 Navigate Menu","41.4.1.3 Arrangement View — Option+2 (Mac) / Alt+2 (Win)"]],["Ableton/Live/UG/41%20Accessibility%20and%20Keyboard%20Nav/04%20Navigating%20in%20Live/01%20Navigate%20Menu/","source-block-2799","Audio clip fades cannot yet be edited with a screen reader.",["41.4.1 Navigate Menu","41.4.1.3 Arrangement View — Option+2 (Mac) / Alt+2 (Win)"]],["Ableton/Live/UG/41%20Accessibility%20and%20Keyboard%20Nav/04%20Navigating%20in%20Live/01%20Navigate%20Menu/","source-block-2863","41.4.1.4 Clip View — Option+3 (Mac) / Alt+3 (Win)",["41.4.1 Navigate Menu"]],["Ableton/Live/UG/41%20Accessibility%20and%20Keyboard%20Nav/04%20Navigating%20in%20Live/01%20Navigate%20Menu/","source-block-2925","Open a clip with a double-click or Cmd+Option+3 (Mac) / Ctrl+Alt+3 (Win). Clip View has clip panels and an editor; Option+Shift+P (Mac) / Alt+Shift+P (Win) focuses the panels and Option+3 focuses the editor.",["41.4.1 Navigate Menu","41.4.1.4 Clip View — Option+3 (Mac) / Alt+3 (Win)"]],["Ableton/Live/UG/41%20Accessibility%20and%20Keyboard%20Nav/04%20Navigating%20in%20Live/01%20Navigate%20Menu/","source-block-3147","MIDI Note Editor — turn on Options → MIDI Note Editor Preview to hear notes as you edit. Shift plus left or right selects time; Enter selects the notes in it; Option plus left or right (Mac) moves to the previous or next note boundary.",["41.4.1 Navigate Menu","41.4.1.4 Clip View — Option+3 (Mac) / Alt+3 (Win)"]],["Ableton/Live/UG/41%20Accessibility%20and%20Keyboard%20Nav/04%20Navigating%20in%20Live/01%20Navigate%20Menu/","source-block-3401","Moving between notes — Option plus up or down (Mac) jumps to the previous or next note; Option plus left or right jumps to the previous or next note of the same pitch; add Shift to extend the selection.",["41.4.1 Navigate Menu","41.4.1.4 Clip View — Option+3 (Mac) / Alt+3 (Win)"]],["Ableton/Live/UG/41%20Accessibility%20and%20Keyboard%20Nav/04%20Navigating%20in%20Live/01%20Navigate%20Menu/","source-block-3620","Editing notes — up and down transpose; Shift plus up or down transposes by octave; Shift plus left or right changes length by the grid; left and right move by the grid; Cmd plus up or down changes velocity; Cmd+Option plus up or down changes probability (Mac).",["41.4.1 Navigate Menu","41.4.1.4 Clip View — Option+3 (Mac) / Alt+3 (Win)"]],["Ableton/Live/UG/41%20Accessibility%20and%20Keyboard%20Nav/04%20Navigating%20in%20Live/01%20Navigate%20Menu/","source-block-3899","Audio clips — Option plus left or right moves the insert marker; Shift plus arrows selects time; left and right move a selected Warp Marker; Cmd+I inserts a Warp Marker; Cmd+Shift+I inserts a transient (Mac; Ctrl on Windows).",["41.4.1 Navigate Menu","41.4.1.4 Clip View — Option+3 (Mac) / Alt+3 (Win)"]],["Ableton/Live/UG/41%20Accessibility%20and%20Keyboard%20Nav/04%20Navigating%20in%20Live/01%20Navigate%20Menu/","source-block-4145","MPE editing is not yet supported with screen readers.",["41.4.1 Navigate Menu","41.4.1.4 Clip View — Option+3 (Mac) / Alt+3 (Win)"]],["Ableton/Live/UG/41%20Accessibility%20and%20Keyboard%20Nav/04%20Navigating%20in%20Live/01%20Navigate%20Menu/","source-block-4203","41.4.1.5 Device View — Option+4 (Mac) / Alt+4 (Win)",["41.4.1 Navigate Menu"]],["Ableton/Live/UG/41%20Accessibility%20and%20Keyboard%20Nav/04%20Navigating%20in%20Live/01%20Navigate%20Menu/","source-block-4267","Shows a track's device chain. MIDI tracks hold MIDI effects, instruments and audio effects; audio, group, return and Main tracks hold audio effects.",["41.4.1 Navigate Menu","41.4.1.5 Device View — Option+4 (Mac) / Alt+4 (Win)"]],["Ableton/Live/UG/41%20Accessibility%20and%20Keyboard%20Nav/04%20Navigating%20in%20Live/01%20Navigate%20Menu/","source-block-4420","Each device reads as a group to screen readers. Left and right arrows move between devices, Tab / Shift+Tab through a device's controls, and the usual cut, copy, paste, duplicate and Delete shortcuts work on devices.",["41.4.1 Navigate Menu","41.4.1.5 Device View — Option+4 (Mac) / Alt+4 (Win)"]],["Ableton/Live/UG/41%20Accessibility%20and%20Keyboard%20Nav/04%20Navigating%20in%20Live/01%20Navigate%20Menu/","source-block-4647","Complex devices are not yet fully optimized for screen readers.",["41.4.1 Navigate Menu","41.4.1.5 Device View — Option+4 (Mac) / Alt+4 (Win)"]],["Ableton/Live/UG/41%20Accessibility%20and%20Keyboard%20Nav/04%20Navigating%20in%20Live/01%20Navigate%20Menu/","source-block-4715","41.4.1.6 Browser — Option+5 (Mac) / Alt+5 (Win)",["41.4.1 Navigate Menu"]],["Ableton/Live/UG/41%20Accessibility%20and%20Keyboard%20Nav/04%20Navigating%20in%20Live/01%20Navigate%20Menu/","source-block-4775","The Ableton/Browser has a search bar, filters, a sidebar and a content pane. Cmd+F (Mac) / Ctrl+F (Win) focuses search from anywhere and selects the All label.",["41.4.1 Navigate Menu","41.4.1.6 Browser — Option+5 (Mac) / Alt+5 (Win)"]],["Ableton/Live/UG/41%20Accessibility%20and%20Keyboard%20Nav/04%20Navigating%20in%20Live/01%20Navigate%20Menu/","source-block-4947","Tab moves from search to the filter toggle, the Filter View menu and the sidebar, then to filters or the content pane; down arrow jumps from search to results.",["41.4.1 Navigate Menu","41.4.1.6 Browser — Option+5 (Mac) / Alt+5 (Win)"]],["Ableton/Live/UG/41%20Accessibility%20and%20Keyboard%20Nav/04%20Navigating%20in%20Live/01%20Navigate%20Menu/","source-block-5113","In the sidebar, up and down move between labels and left and right move between sidebar and content. In the content pane, Shift plus up or down multi-selects, and right and left expand and collapse folders.",["41.4.1 Navigate Menu","41.4.1.6 Browser — Option+5 (Mac) / Alt+5 (Win)"]],["Ableton/Live/UG/41%20Accessibility%20and%20Keyboard%20Nav/04%20Navigating%20in%20Live/01%20Navigate%20Menu/","source-block-5326","Turn on Options → Browser File Preview to hear previews; with it off, right arrow still plays the selected item's preview.",["41.4.1 Navigate Menu","41.4.1.6 Browser — Option+5 (Mac) / Alt+5 (Win)"]],["Ableton/Live/UG/41%20Accessibility%20and%20Keyboard%20Nav/04%20Navigating%20in%20Live/01%20Navigate%20Menu/","source-block-5455","Filtering and tagging are not yet supported with screen readers.",["41.4.1 Navigate Menu","41.4.1.6 Browser — Option+5 (Mac) / Alt+5 (Win)"]],["Ableton/Live/UG/41%20Accessibility%20and%20Keyboard%20Nav/04%20Navigating%20in%20Live/01%20Navigate%20Menu/","source-block-5524","41.4.1.7 Groove Pool — Option+6 (Mac) / Alt+6 (Win)",["41.4.1 Navigate Menu"]],["Ableton/Live/UG/41%20Accessibility%20and%20Keyboard%20Nav/04%20Navigating%20in%20Live/01%20Navigate%20Menu/","source-block-5588","Grooves change the timing and feel of clips. In the Groove Pool, Tab / Shift+Tab move between groove parameters and up and down arrows change values.",["41.4.1 Navigate Menu","41.4.1.7 Groove Pool — Option+6 (Mac) / Alt+6 (Win)"]],["Ableton/Live/UG/41%20Accessibility%20and%20Keyboard%20Nav/04%20Navigating%20in%20Live/01%20Navigate%20Menu/","source-block-5746","41.4.1.8 Learn View — Option+7 (Mac) / Alt+7 (Win)",["41.4.1 Navigate Menu"]],["Ableton/Live/UG/41%20Accessibility%20and%20Keyboard%20Nav/04%20Navigating%20in%20Live/01%20Navigate%20Menu/","source-block-5809","Short lessons on different parts of Live.",["41.4.1 Navigate Menu","41.4.1.8 Learn View — Option+7 (Mac) / Alt+7 (Win)"]],["Ableton/Live/UG/41%20Accessibility%20and%20Keyboard%20Nav/05%20Editing%20Automation%20and%20Modulation%20Envelopes/","source-block-197","41.5 Editing Automation and Modulation Envelopes",[]],["Ableton/Live/UG/41%20Accessibility%20and%20Keyboard%20Nav/05%20Editing%20Automation%20and%20Modulation%20Envelopes/","source-block-378","Breakpoints in automation and modulation envelopes can be added, edited and deleted from the keyboard, with screen reader feedback. This works in Arrangement automation lanes and in a clip's Envelope Editor.",["41.5 Editing Automation and Modulation Envelopes"]],["Ableton/Live/UG/41%20Accessibility%20and%20Keyboard%20Nav/05%20Editing%20Automation%20and%20Modulation%20Envelopes/01%20Navigating%20Between%20Breakpoints/","source-block-306","41.5.1 Navigating Between Breakpoints",[]],["Ableton/Live/UG/41%20Accessibility%20and%20Keyboard%20Nav/05%20Editing%20Automation%20and%20Modulation%20Envelopes/01%20Navigating%20Between%20Breakpoints/","source-block-463","Left and right arrows move the insert marker along the envelope, showing the value at each point.",["41.5.1 Navigating Between Breakpoints"]],["Ableton/Live/UG/41%20Accessibility%20and%20Keyboard%20Nav/05%20Editing%20Automation%20and%20Modulation%20Envelopes/01%20Navigating%20Between%20Breakpoints/","source-block-720","Enter creates a breakpoint at the insert marker; press Enter again to place it, or move it with the arrows first.",["41.5.1 Navigating Between Breakpoints"]],["Ableton/Live/UG/41%20Accessibility%20and%20Keyboard%20Nav/05%20Editing%20Automation%20and%20Modulation%20Envelopes/01%20Navigating%20Between%20Breakpoints/","source-block-841","Option plus left or right (Mac) / Alt plus left or right (Win) jumps to the previous or next breakpoint. The focused breakpoint takes the same color as a mouse hover.",["41.5.1 Navigating Between Breakpoints"]],["Ableton/Live/UG/41%20Accessibility%20and%20Keyboard%20Nav/05%20Editing%20Automation%20and%20Modulation%20Envelopes/02%20Selecting%20and%20Editing%20Breakpoints/","source-block-473","41.5.2 Selecting and Editing Breakpoints",[]],["Ableton/Live/UG/41%20Accessibility%20and%20Keyboard%20Nav/05%20Editing%20Automation%20and%20Modulation%20Envelopes/02%20Selecting%20and%20Editing%20Breakpoints/","source-block-636","Enter selects the breakpoint at the insert marker; Option-click (Mac) / Alt-click (Win) moves the marker to a breakpoint and selects it; Tab / Shift+Tab select the next or previous one. A selected breakpoint pulses.",["41.5.2 Selecting and Editing Breakpoints"]],["Ableton/Live/UG/41%20Accessibility%20and%20Keyboard%20Nav/05%20Editing%20Automation%20and%20Modulation%20Envelopes/02%20Selecting%20and%20Editing%20Breakpoints/","source-block-865","After undoing a breakpoint move with Cmd+Z (Mac) / Ctrl+Z (Win), the restored breakpoint briefly takes the hover color, which helps when breakpoints line up vertically.",["41.5.2 Selecting and Editing Breakpoints"]],["Ableton/Live/UG/41%20Accessibility%20and%20Keyboard%20Nav/05%20Editing%20Automation%20and%20Modulation%20Envelopes/02%20Selecting%20and%20Editing%20Breakpoints/","source-block-1041","Type a number or use up and down to change the value; Enter confirms and deselects, Esc cancels. Delete removes the breakpoint.",["41.5.2 Selecting and Editing Breakpoints"]],["Ableton/Live/UG/41%20Accessibility%20and%20Keyboard%20Nav/05%20Editing%20Automation%20and%20Modulation%20Envelopes/03%20Switching%20Between%20Automation%20Envelopes%20in%20Arrangement%20View/","source-block-306","41.5.3 Switching Between Automation Envelopes in Arrangement View",[]],["Ableton/Live/UG/41%20Accessibility%20and%20Keyboard%20Nav/05%20Editing%20Automation%20and%20Modulation%20Envelopes/03%20Switching%20Between%20Automation%20Envelopes%20in%20Arrangement%20View/","source-block-519","Option plus up or down (Mac) / Alt plus up or down (Win) cycles through a track's automation envelopes in the Arrangement.",["41.5.3 Switching Between Automation Envelopes in Arrangement View"]],["Ableton/Live/UG/41%20Accessibility%20and%20Keyboard%20Nav/05%20Editing%20Automation%20and%20Modulation%20Envelopes/03%20Switching%20Between%20Automation%20Envelopes%20in%20Arrangement%20View/","source-block-649","Add Shift to cycle through every device parameter, automated or not.",["41.5.3 Switching Between Automation Envelopes in Arrangement View"]],["Ableton/Live/UG/42%20Keyboard%20Shortcuts/","source-block-180","42. Live Keyboard Shortcuts",[]],["Ableton/Live/UG/42%20Keyboard%20Shortcuts/","source-block-282","Keyboard shortcuts grouped by task, from showing views to editing envelopes and clips.",["42. Live Keyboard Shortcuts"]],["Ableton/Live/UG/42%20Keyboard%20Shortcuts/","source-block-1051","Live 11 notes: Ableton/Manual/36/7 Loop Brace Start End Markers",["42. Live Keyboard Shortcuts"]],["Ableton/Live/UG/42%20Keyboard%20Shortcuts/01%20Showing%20and%